 "extra_unmapped": [],
 "conversion_needs": [
  "Overall composition mol% (H2O, NaCl, CO2) per sub-table; to get x_CO2 on a salt-free basis use CO2/(CO2+H2O); molality of NaCl = NaCl/(H2O*0.018015) mol/kg.",
  "'6 weight% relative to water' is consistent with the printed mol% only if read as 6 g NaCl per 100 g of the CO2-free NaCl solution (NaCl/H2O mole ratio 1.93/97.90 = 0.0197, = 0.06/0.94 x 18.015/58.44); likewise 10 and 20 weight% (mass fraction in the salt solution). The printed mol% values are the primary composition.",
  "V cm3/mol -> m3/mol x 1e-6."
 ],
 "notes": "Side-by-side blocks (three printed columns) stacked in printed order: left column top to bottom (sub-tables 1-7), middle column (8-15), right column (16-24); numbering 1-24 assigned by this order, which matches the title (last four = 10 and 20 weight%). Each label row carries the three printed mol% values. Rows within a sub-table kept in printed order (not monotonic in places, e.g. sub-table 4 rows 19.0/423 then 20.0/456; sub-table 17 rows 55.4/621/95.0 then 58.5/621/82.5). Not a direct phase-composition measurement: water-rich isopleths are bubble-point-like (solubility of CO2 in brine at the boundary), CO2-rich isopleths dew-point-like; above the critical curve the side is undefined. Builder should treat as 'other' unless a phase-side rule is added."
}